  "verification": "The shared-request architecture, corrected FD50/FD51 switch bytes, both real P1L hooks, standalone hysteresis, separate launch/standalone fixed-IPW selection, cut-active adaptation freeze, the shared roughness/misfire-detection and coil/resistor cleanup guard, exact coil/resistor DTC descriptors, and post-release DTC maturation pass the canonical MS41.0 exact-byte execution gate. MS41.0 has per-cylinder roughness/misfire detection, but its stock descriptor table has no dedicated DTC 238-243 entries. Vehicle validation remains required.",
  "title": "Ignition Cut",
  "user_description": "Adds an independent MS41.0 ignition-cut limiter with corrected pin inputs and its own adjustable RPM hysteresis and fixed injector pulse width while cutting.",
  "description": "MS41.0 Ignition Cut V9. E847.0 owns the standalone limiter request and E847.1 is reserved for Launch Control V7. Pins 80/81 read FD51.1/.0 and pin 82 reads FD50.7, matching the MS41.0 input latch. CUT_HYST and CUT_IPW apply only to the standalone limiter; Launch Control V7 supplies separate LC_HYST and LC_IPW settings, and LC_IPW wins while both spark requests are active. Hysteresis is RPM/32, fixed IPW is uint16 x0.00534 ms, and FF/FFFF select zero hysteresis/stock injection. While E847.0/.1/.2 reports a real cut, trim stores pause and the homologous lambda, upstream O2-voltage, shared roughness/misfire-detection, and coil/resistor paths take their stock disabled cleanup routes. MS41.0 has per-cylinder roughness/misfire detection, but its stock descriptor table has no dedicated DTC 238-243 entries.",
